"prose": [
{
"from": 199,
"to": 214,
"text": "**The gates:** - blitz-dom's unit tests (gate 1); - the engine check, red before step 2 (gate 2); - seven_guis' lib tests: the parse's unit test and the stand's inline boots (gate 3); - the sample check, red before step 3's carriage (gate 4); - the cross-OS table with its new row (gate 5); - the readers that open Circle Drawer or hold a widget, which must read as predicted (gate 6); - the whole of blitz-tests per package (gate 7); - seven_guis' package tests, its process checks included, so the binary that now holds the widget still answers   (gate 8); - the lock probe, four lines added, none removed against the commit this chunk starts from (gate 9); - the pre-push gate `fast` (gate 10), whose workspace tests, both clippy lines and `embolden` read the engine change   and the widget's glyph paint; - the `build` leg, which builds seven_guis for `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with the widget's crates (gate 11); - the `audit` leg, since the lock moves (gate 12; security-plan · dependency-security/decision/dependency-audit-cargo-deny); - `stand-repeat`, which takes both new `stand_` files by their prefix (gate 13)."
},
{
"from": 216,
"to": 222,
"text": "**What no step changes:** no served task, kept check or committed check (F1 A), so `stand_cross_os_readings`' table, `host_log`, `mcp_log` and the cold-agent pipe move nothing; all of them are read inside `fast` and `stand-repeat`. No log site, span or field. No public item or public doc comment: `widget_click_synthesis` is private, so the `doc` leg is not listed. No a11y leg file: the new checks read role and name through the snapshot, no AccessKit tree test, so they meet none of the leg's criteria (test-plan · ci-integration/decision/a11y-leg-membership); the leg's file count, which the capability pin reads, does not move. No boot path of a binary changes, and no served task holds the sample, so there is no smoke entry. There is no live leg and no headful self-verify on this project."
},
{
"from": 224,
"to": 225,
"text": "**Controls.** Each new check reads red before the code it guards (steps 1 and 6), and under step 10's one-shot `gate.py control`; gate 9 reads `0+0` on the untouched tree. No other new control."
},
{
"from": 227,
"to": 230,
"text": "**What CI reads.** The acceptance needs CI's three hosts to read the sample's canvas digest equal (gate 5 inside each host's test leg). The diff is not OS-sensitive otherwise: no OS `cfg` site is added (the added `cfg` is the `custom-widget` feature's). The canvas's glyphs are drawn by the widget, and widget glyph runs read byte-equal on the three hosts (`stand_canvas_cross_os`, «Hg», CI#45209188300). The operator's hygiene, push and CI entries stand."
}
],
